docs {
  Submit a signed transaction for execution on mainnet.

  **Service:** `sui.rpc.v2.TransactionExecutionService` · **Method:** `ExecuteTransaction` (unary)

  **⚠️ Not live-tested.** Unlike every other request in this folder, this
  one broadcasts a real, irreversible transaction and moves real funds /
  mutates real on-chain state, so it wasn't run against mainnet while
  verifying this collection — doing so would have required signing with
  a live private key. The request/response shapes below are taken
  directly from the vendored `transaction_execution_service.proto`, not
  from a live response.

  **Request fields:**
  - `transaction` (Transaction): the transaction to execute. `bcs.value`
    is the BCS-encoded `TransactionData`, base64-encoded for the gRPC-JSON
    body (or populate `transaction.kind`/`sender`/`gas_payment`/
    `expiration` directly instead of `bcs`).
  - `signatures` (repeated UserSignature): one signature per required
    signer, authorizing `transaction`.
  - `read_mask` (optional FieldMask): defaults to `effects.status,checkpoint`.

  Before using this, build and sign a real transaction with the Sui SDK
  (or `sui client`), and only run it against an address/network you
  intend to spend from. Consider testing on `sui-testnet.g.alchemy.com`
  first.
}
